{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_adr_adr_023_asset_register", "label": "ADR-023 The asset register follows the CMDB (asset 0.2.0, event 0.3.0, GraphQL 1.0.0)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-023-asset-register.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_023_asset_register_owned_ci_types", "label": "OWNED_CI_TYPES", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-023-asset-register.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Names the CI types that are property, licences or subscriptions; addresses, interfaces, records, rules, workloads, sites, accounts and vendors are topology or context, not assets."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_023_asset_register_asset_per_owned_ci", "label": "One asset per owned CI, kept by the reconciler persist()", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-023-asset-register.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Syed's review: 'asset management is also dummy, just showing planned'. persist() creates a register row (source discovery, stage deployed) in the same transaction as the CI and refreshes discovery-observed fields on update: a reported value replaces, an unreported one leaves the row alone, vendor cover is replaced only while it still comes from a vendor API, never over a person's entry. One array statement per batch keeps the sweep budget; unique index (tenant, ciId) makes it idempotent. Dates are taken as observed; a missing date is a data gap, nothing is invented."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_023_asset_register_asset_fields_from_ci", "label": "assetFieldsFromCi (contract mapping)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-023-asset-register.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lives in the contract package so the reconciler, the API and migration 0015's one-off backfill agree. Tag prefers attributes.assetTag, then the CI code, then the CI id."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_023_asset_register_asset_data_gaps", "label": "assetDataGaps / AssetDataGap / assetSummary", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-023-asset-register.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Data gaps are first-class: which of warranty, support and end of life a row lacks; register filters on them, summary counts them per layer beside expired cover. supportEndsAt resolves either a SupportContract row (ADR-005) or the asset's own support entry."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_023_asset_register_update_asset", "label": "Mutation.updateAsset (manual entry, audited)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-023-asset-register.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each changed field is an asset_audits row and openmap.asset.updated lists the fields; cover a person enters is stamped manual and verified now."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_023_asset_register_create_asset", "label": "Mutation.createAsset (CI through the outbox + register row)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-023-asset-register.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Records equipment discovery cannot see by creating a CI of the chosen type through the outbox (graph and search carry it) and the register row with it (source manual), so the CMDB stays the single record."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_023_asset_register_diagnose_unknown", "label": "diagnoseUnknown rule-based diagnosis", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-023-asset-register.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Power equipment answering SNMP goes to the DCIM collector scope; SNMP-answering device needs a credential; open port outside the well-known set is an unknown application needing agent/SSH credential or a label; no SNMP, no web interface, no open port is a device without out-of-band management, manual entry only; not seen for ASSETS.unknownStaleDays is stale. Each row carries evidence and a suggested layer and type that preset the label panel."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_023_asset_register_ensure_asset_for_ci", "label": "ensureAssetForCi (called by labelCi)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-023-asset-register.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Labelling a CI into an owned type creates its register row at once so the person then fills the cover dates."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_023_asset_register_asset_events", "label": "openmap.asset.created / openmap.asset.updated (event 0.3.0)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-023-asset-register.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_023_asset_register_graphql_1_0_0", "label": "GraphQL 1.0.0 (nullable manufacturer/model breaking change)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-023-asset-register.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "AssetRecord.manufacturer and model become nullable because a software instance or cloud resource has neither; a breaking change, hence the major bump."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_023_asset_register_asset_retirement", "label": "Asset retirement follows CI retirement (REQ-DISC-030)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-023-asset-register.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No path retires CIs automatically yet; when the stale sweep lands an asset follows its CI to retired. A replay reset deletes discovery-sourced rows with their CIs and keeps plan and manual rows."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_023_asset_register_req_cmdb_039", "label": "REQ-CMDB-039", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-023-asset-register.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_023_asset_register_req_cmdb_040", "label": "REQ-CMDB-040", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-023-asset-register.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_adr_adr_023_asset_register", "target": "docs_adr_adr_023_asset_register_owned_ci_types", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-023-asset-register.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_adr_023_asset_register", "target": "docs_adr_adr_023_asset_register_asset_per_owned_ci", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-023-asset-register.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_adr_023_asset_register_asset_per_owned_ci", "target": "docs_adr_adr_023_asset_register_owned_ci_types", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-023-asset-register.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_adr_023_asset_register_asset_per_owned_ci", "target": "docs_adr_adr_023_asset_register_asset_fields_from_ci", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-023-asset-register.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_adr_023_asset_register_asset_fields_from_ci", "target": "docs_adr_adr_014_ci_short_codes_cicode